      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the test. Let me write an improved version with better variable names, a descriptive test method name, and explanatory comments.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses descriptive variable names (`backingList`, `nullKeyTransformer`, `indexedCollection`, `changed`), a self-documenting method name, and explanatory comments that clarify the non-obvious behavior — namely that `removeAll` delegates removal to the backing list, so the argument collection ends up emptied as a side effect."
